<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap prose" style="max-width:760px">
    <p>Made Out of Clay Productions wants parents, caregivers, educators, and young readers to be able to use this website comfortably. We are working toward the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 Level AA.</p>

    <h2>What we have built in</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Semantic headings, landmarks, skip links, labels, and descriptive image text.</li>
      <li>Keyboard-visible focus, keyboard-operable controls, and generous touch targets.</li>
      <li>Layouts that reflow on smaller screens and at increased text sizes.</li>
      <li>Reduced-motion behavior for optional animation.</li>
      <li>Visible controls for video and read-along media. The complete <a href="/read/titus-and-the-lions/">Titus story text</a> appears on the page alongside its media.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Need another format or found a barrier?</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}?subject=Accessibility%20help">{{ site.email }}</a> with the page address and what you were trying to do. We will respond as soon as we can and can provide book or site information in another reasonable format.</p>

    <h2>Ongoing work</h2>
    <p>Accessibility is an ongoing practice, not a one-time score. We review new pages and interactive features as the site changes and prioritize barriers that prevent someone from reading, navigating, contacting us, or reaching a free story.</p>
  </div>
</section>
